# IMPORTANT — file-naming clarification:
# 1. Liquidity OWN content (their source, configs, brand assets, IP they
#    own) does NOT belong here — lives under ~/work/liquidity/* only.
# 2. Lux WORK PRODUCT *ABOUT* Liquidity (enforcement memos, license
#    audits, board materials, IP-theft documentation) DOES belong here.
#    Those files commonly have LIQUIDITY_* or *Liquidity* in the name.
# This .gitignore therefore does NOT block LIQUIDITY_* / SATSCHEL_*
# filenames as a class — humans must judge per-file at git-add time.
liquidity/exhibits/LiquiditySwap.mp4
liquidity/exhibits/Alpaca - liquidity.io*.zip

# liquidity/exhibits/alpaca-liquidity-bd/ — Counterparty's Alpaca clearing-BD
# diligence materials including KYC ID jpegs (Eric Choi front/back), signed
# beneficial-ownership certifications, and other PII-sensitive evidence.
# Preserved on disk for counsel reference; deliberately NOT committed to
# git history due to PII content + push-size concerns. Counsel may produce
# specific files on subpoena/discovery from the on-disk preservation.
liquidity/exhibits/alpaca-liquidity-bd/
